  "scope": "Flower petal record layout, selection and drag naming, and settled-state interpretation.",
  "changes": [
    "Replace the untyped 0x2c0-byte mArray with 22 plain Petal records. Share that record with the retained PetalView instead of duplicating its layout.",
    "Correct the angle to s16 with two padding bytes and replace misleading grabX/grabY names with touchStartX/touchStartY. Add a 0x20 record-size assertion; retain the 0x5ff8 scene-size assertion.",
    "Name mPetalsSettled and clarify selection, dragging, shuffle and resource-loading locals. Change plain screen-vector second-coordinate spelling from z to y.",
    "Correct comments: selection uses the first eligible petal within range, preferring attached petals; the streak counts completed rounds. Remove the stale volatile-counter description from StartRound."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "petal_layout": "The per-frame view establishes active/released/held/counted bytes, x/y at +4/+8, driftX/fallSpeed at +0xc/+0x10. Behavior writes the current cursor to +0x14/+0x18 on pickup; these are initial touch coordinates, not grab offsets. DealPetals stores and swaps a 16-bit angle at +0x1c; Render reads the same halfword. No observed member occupies the last two bytes.",
    "lifecycle": "The nested Petal is trivial, with scalar fields and no constructor/destructor. The scene retains the explicit Petal_ElemCtor/Petal_ElemDtor callbacks in __cxa_vec_ctor/__cxa_vec_cleanup. The existing nontrivial Vec2 remains a local shuffle temporary only; putting it in Petal would introduce implicit destruction. Entire object comparison proves no additional lifecycle output was emitted.",
    "settled_and_selection": "UpdatePetals initializes settled to one and clears it for active held/attached/falling petals. Behavior gates its result sequence on the corresponding +0x5fcd byte. The first selection scan excludes released petals and breaks at the first distance below 0x18000; the fallback scan permits already released petals.",
    "ownership": "Queue20 state 466f7b7436b71e6ce75368547cb96829fa7a615e: no active Flower class/file resources or overlapping ov006 ranges 0x0212a554..0x0212b890. This complete text range is enrolled in config/arm9/overlays/ov006/delinks.txt.",
    "runtime_validation": "No emulator run was needed for these names: they follow explicit loads/stores and selection/math conditions. No new original spelling, petal artwork identity or opaque face-object layout is asserted.",
    "retained_constraints": [
      "Keep the measured PetalView and A1/A2/B1/W1/W2 address launders, raw indexed spellings, declaration lifetimes, and Render row views.",
      "Keep the nontrivial Vec2 local shuffle temporary and its stack slot, all pragmas and source function ordering.",
      "Keep the explicit lifecycle ABI callbacks, opaque face-object storage and constructor/destructor variant manifests unchanged."
    ]
